Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plain_drm: handle duplicate frames

Libretro cores may pass a null frame pointer to request duplication of the
previous video frame. PCSX-ReARMed and FinalBurn Neo both do this during
startup. The plain DRM backend dereferences the pointer unconditionally and
crashes. Keep the current scanout buffer for duplicate frames.
---
 gfx/drivers/drm_gfx.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/gfx/drivers/drm_gfx.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers/drm_gfx.c
@@ -787,6 +787,10 @@ static bool drm_frame(void *data, const void *frame, unsigned width,
    menu_driver_frame(menu_is_alive, video_info);
 #endif
 
+   /* A null frame is libretro's request to duplicate the last frame. */
+   if (!frame)
+      return true;
+
    /* Update main surface: locate free page, blit and flip. */
    drm_surface_update(_drmvars, frame, _drmvars->main_surface);
    /* The menu owns the single plane until it closes. */
